# Baseline recorded on the code as it was BEFORE #316 (tree cc4c808), from src/config/validate/testdata/validators_sink.json.
# Format: [conditions] text, in emission order; a condition is a root feature that must be on (jwt) or off (!jwt).
# See golden_tests.rs. Do not edit by hand; a refactor must never need to change this file.
[redis,consumers] warning|rateLimit.store|multiple distinct Redis URLs configured across site/route/consumer rateLimit.store fields (redis://127.0.0.1:6379, redis://a:6379, redis://site-host:6379, redis://route-host:6379, redis://consumer-host:6379, redis://***@site-host:6379, redis://a\\nfake log line: [ERROR] pwned:6379). Only one Redis connection is ever established per process — Conduit will connect to 'redis://127.0.0.1:6379' and every other level configuring a different URL will silently share that same connection instead of getting its own. Point every level at the same Redis instance to avoid surprises.
[redis,!consumers] warning|rateLimit.store|multiple distinct Redis URLs configured across site/route/consumer rateLimit.store fields (redis://127.0.0.1:6379, redis://a:6379, redis://site-host:6379, redis://route-host:6379, redis://***@site-host:6379, redis://a\\nfake log line: [ERROR] pwned:6379). Only one Redis connection is ever established per process — Conduit will connect to 'redis://127.0.0.1:6379' and every other level configuring a different URL will silently share that same connection instead of getting its own. Point every level at the same Redis instance to avoid surprises.
[] error|sites[2].tls|Cannot combine 'acme' with 'cert'/'key' — use Auto-TLS or manual certificates, not both
[] error|sites[3].tls|TLS 'cert' and 'key' must both be set — 'key' is missing
[] error|sites[6].tls.versions|tls.versions is not currently enforced — Pingora 0.9's rustls TLS backend gives Conduit no API to restrict protocol versions (TLS 1.2 and 1.3 are always both enabled). Remove this field; see https://github.com/lopatnov/conduit/issues/189 for status.
[] error|sites[7].tls.ciphers|tls.ciphers is not currently enforced — Pingora 0.9's rustls TLS backend gives Conduit no API to restrict cipher suites (the default rustls suite set is always used). Remove this field; see https://github.com/lopatnov/conduit/issues/189 for status.
